<p>Richard Garfield, creator of <em>Magic: The Gathering</em>, offered this innovative problem at the <a href="https://wpc.puzzles.com/history/2000.htm">Ninth World Puzzle Championship</a> in 2000:</p>
<p>&#8220;Add the weights and balloons to the diagram so that the entire mechanism is in equilibrium. As with normal balance puzzles, the total torque at each fulcrum must be zero.&#8221; The weights and balloons can be attached only at the designated blue points. Each beam is graduated, though that can be a bit hard to see here &#8212; click to enlarge.</p>
